:164},[154,2013,2014],{"class":264},"\"{}\"",[154,2016,321],{"class":164},[154,2018,2019],{"class":171},"checksum",[154,2021,366],{"class":164},[154,2023,796],{"class":160},[154,2025,2026],{"class":164},"data));\n",[154,2028,2030],{"class":156,"line":2029},12,[154,2031,1957],{"class":164},[2033,2034,2035,2039,2058,2096,2099,2182],"details",{},[2036,2037,2038],"summary",{},"Answer",[462,2040,2041,2042,2044,2045,1725,2048,2050,2051,2054,2055,1785],{},"In a ",[305,2043,307],{}," build, this panics: ",[51,2046,2047],{},"attempt to add with overflow",[305,2049,313],{}," build, it silently prints ",[51,2052,2053],{},"94"," (the wrapped result of ",[51,2056,2057],{},"(200 + 100 + 50) % 256",[462,2059,2060,2063,2064,2066,2067,2069,2070,2073,2074,2076,2077,2080,2081,2084,2085,2087,2088,2091,2092,2095],{},[51,2061,2062],{},"200 + 100 = 300",", which overflows ",[51,2065,57],{},"'s range (0–255) on the very first addition. Rust's ",[51,2068,1225],{}," operator has different behavior depending on build profile specifically for this case: debug builds insert overflow checks that panic immediately (",[51,2071,2072],{},"overflow-checks = true"," by default in the dev profile), while release builds compile the same ",[51,2075,1939],{}," to a two's-complement wraparound with no check at all (",[51,2078,2079],{},"overflow-checks = false"," by default in the release profile) — this is a deliberate performance\u002Fsafety tradeoff, not an inconsistency, but it means the ",[643,2082,2083],{},"exact same source code"," produces a hard crash in one build mode and a silently wrong numeric answer in the other. A function like ",[51,2086,2019],{}," that looks correct and passes casual testing in ",[51,2089,2090],{},"cargo run"," (debug, which would actually panic and get noticed) can ship a silent miscalculation in ",[51,2093,2094],{},"cargo run --release"," if the overflow case wasn't covered by a test that runs in both modes.",[462,2097,2098],{},"The fix is to be explicit about the desired overflow behavior rather than relying on ambient build-profile behavior:",[142,2100,2101],{"language":144},[146,2102,2104],{"className":148,"code":2103,"language":144,"meta":150,"style":150},"fn checksum(values: &[u8]) -> u8 {\n    values.iter().fold(0u8, |acc, &v| acc.wrapping_add(v))\n}\n",[51,2105,2106,2130,2178],{"__ignoreMap":150},[154,2107,2108,2110,2112,2114,2116,2118,2120,2122,2124,2126,2128],{"class":156,"line":157},[154,2109,1195],{"class":160},[154,2111,1872],{"class":171},[154,2113,1875],{"class":164},[154,2115,168],{"class":160},[154,2117,1014],{"class":160},[154,2119,1165],{"class":164},[154,2121,57],{"class":171},[154,2123,1886],{"class":164},[154,2125,1217],{"class":160},[154,2127,198],{"class":171},[154,2129,1893],{"class":164},[154,2131,2132,2135,2137,2140,2142,2144,2147,2149,2151,2153,2155,2158,2161,2163,2166,2168,2171,2173,2175],{"class":156,"line":188},[154,2133,2134],{"class":164},"    values",[154,2136,339],{"class":160},[154,2138,2139],{"class":171},"iter",[154,2141,888],{"class":164},[154,2143,339],{"class":160},[154,2145,2146],{"class":171},"fold",[154,2148,366],{"class":164},[154,2150,852],{"class":181},[154,2152,57],{"class":171},[154,2154,321],{"class":164},[154,2156,2157],{"class":160},"|",[154,2159,2160],{"class":164},"acc, ",[154,2162,796],{"class":160},[154,2164,2165],{"class":164},"v",[154,2167,2157],{"class":160},[154,2169,2170],{"class":164}," acc",[154,2172,339],{"class":160},[154,2174,320],{"class":171},[154,2176,2177],{"class":164},"(v))\n",[154,2179,2180],{"class":156,"line":208},[154,2181,1957],{"class":164},[462,2183,2184,2187,2188,474,2190,474,2192,2194],{},[305,2185,2186],{},"The lesson",": integer overflow panics in debug builds but silently wraps in release builds — code that \"worked\" during development can compute a different, wrong answer in production unless overflow-prone arithmetic uses explicit ",[51,2189,1621],{},[51,2191,1615],{},[51,2193,1618],{}," methods.",[14,2196,2197],{"id":2036},"Summary",[462,2199,2200